From f35296be89127faca62696583be33d99131aa8e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: guanxiongsun <sungx.cs@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:12:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Move deleted objects offscreen on the CPU path

On the CPU pipeline, delete_scene_object removes a rigid or geometry
object with destroy(), which hides it and disables its gravity but
leaves the prim where it is, with its collision shapes still enabled.
Every later layout in the process then holds invisible obstacles where
earlier episodes left their objects. Objects placed there are pushed
aside and the layout fails the stability check: swap_blocks, whose
cubes always sit on one of three mats, lost 5 of its first 7 layouts,
each of which settles in a fresh process. Leftovers that stay put
remain in the robot's way during the episode.

Move the object offscreen before destroying it, as relocate_stale_objects
does for the objects it keeps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 env/scene_manager/scene_manager.py | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/env/scene_manager/scene_manager.py b/env/scene_manager/scene_manager.py
index e81b673..77cc682 100644
--- a/env/scene_manager/scene_manager.py
+++ b/env/scene_manager/scene_manager.py
@@ -722,6 +722,9 @@ class SceneManager:
                     delete_prim(obj.prim_path)
         else:
             if isinstance(obj, RigidObject) or isinstance(obj, GeometryObject):
+                # destroy() keeps the prim in place and its collision shapes enabled; without the
+                # move, it stays an invisible obstacle in every later layout
+                obj.relocate_offscreen()
                 obj.destroy()
             elif isinstance(obj, GarmentObject):
                 if hasattr(obj, "usd_prim_path") and is_prim_path_valid(obj.usd_prim_path):
